## What to deliver

Build and rig the fortress up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a tracked hull carrying a big main turret and
cannon, with a rotating secondary gun turret on each flank. The required interface
is four caller joints — **`main_turret_yaw`** (fine-aim the main turret within a
narrow forward cone) and **`main_gun_pitch`** (elevate the main cannon), plus
**`left_turret_yaw`** and **`right_turret_yaw`**, which traverse the two side
turrets so each covers its own flank arc. Produce **every** required part and joint; you may add your
own extra parts, joints, or auto-play clips on top, but do not drop or contradict
the required interface. When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs
and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
